// Title: Suspicious Diantz Alternate Data Stream Execution
// Sigma ID: 6b369ced-4b1d-48f1-b427-fdc0de0790bd
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-11-26 | Modified: 2022-12-31
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564.004
// Description: Compress target file into a cab file stored in the Alternate Data Stream (ADS) of the target
//   file.
// False positives:
//   - Very Possible
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Diantz/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_diantz_ads.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "diantz.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".cab") and ProcessCommandLine matches regex ":[^\\\\]"
